	(text "Series 1k: protection against\noutput contention and limits\nback-feed when ESP is off"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 79.248 78.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0f45c282-8fad-4015-8abd-95102e9a1faa")
	)
	(text "Additional pin functions:\nhttps://pinout.xyz/"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "36e2c557-2c2a-4fba-9b6f-1167ab8ec281")
	)
	(text "ESP pin  ->  Raspberry Pi (via 1k)\nIO0    ->  GPIO23 (pin 16)\nIO1    ->  GPIO24 (pin 18)\nIO2    ->  GPIO5 (pin 29)  strap, Pi pull-up\nIO3    ->  GPIO25 (pin 22)\nIO4    ->  GPIO12/PWM0 (pin 32)\nIO5    ->  GPIO9/SPI0.MISO (pin 21)\nIO6    ->  GPIO11/SPI0.SCLK (pin 23)\nIO7    ->  GPIO10/SPI0.MOSI (pin 19)\nIO8    ->  GPIO6 (pin 31)  strap, Pi pull-up\nIO9    ->  GPIO4 (pin 7)  BOOT, Pi pull-up\nIO10   ->  GPIO8/SPI0.CE0 (pin 24)\nIO20   ->  GPIO14/TXD0 (pin 8)   ESP RX\nIO21   ->  GPIO15/RXD0 (pin 10)  ESP TX\nPWR    <-  GPIO22 (pin 15)  1 = OFF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "468235a5-37ca-4276-94c4-4f4bae0f288c")
	)
	(text "ESP power switch: ON by default (R16 pulls gate low).\nPi GPIO22 = HIGH -> ESP power OFF. SW1 = manual power cycle\n(C3 Pro Mini has no EN pin).\nDownload mode: GPIO22=1, GPIO4=0, GPIO22=0, then\nesptool --before no_reset --port /dev/serial0 ...\nBefore power-off set Pi pins driving ESP to inputs\n(avoids back-powering ESP through IO)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.146 101.854 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4db90943-7844-4f81-b2b2-76c16ee7b0c1")
	)
	(text "5V pin of ESP is intentionally NC:\nUSB of ESP must not back-feed the Pi"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.486 29.718 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "509d5236-74ab-4889-bf00-7c284992649e")
	)
	(text "ID_SD and ID_SC PINS:\nThese pins are reserved for HAT ID EEPROM.\n\nAt boot time this I2C interface will be\ninterrogated to look for an EEPROM\nthat identifes the attached board and\nallows automagic setup of the GPIOs\n(and optionally, Linux drivers).\n\nBridging JP1 enables write protection.\n\nDO NOT USE these pins for anything other\nthan attaching an I2C ID EEPROM. Leave\nunconnected if ID EEPROM not required."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.146 179.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8714082a-55fe-4a29-9d48-99ae1ef73073")
	)
